<title>SINGAPORE: INDIA TENDERS TO SELL SEPT 8-10 COCHIN HAN NAPHTHA.</title>
<headline>INDIA TENDERS TO SELL SEPT 8-10 COCHIN HAN NAPHTHA.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) from Cochin on the east coast, lifting September 8-10, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes August 21 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last tender for Cochin HAN, lifting July 31-August 2, was awarded to Swiss trader Glencore at around $30 per tonne below U.S. Gulf coast 87-octane gasoline quotes, on a free-on-board (fob) basis, industry sources said.</p>
